# Sandbox-tool refusal markers. Some sandboxed test runners wrap
# `exec`, refuse the call, and drop a marker file shaped like
# `,<hex>.<digits>` (e.g. `,19ea827b1e7.671531`) in the cwd
# of the refused process. The `tests/nq_cli.rs` harness now
# smoke-checks the resolved nq binary so the wrapper's output no
# longer reaches the test, but the marker files still appear
# whenever an exec is refused. The leading comma is the anchor —
# no normal repo artifact starts with `,`.
,[0-9a-f]*.[0-9]*
